                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "664b7f94-03c9-3354-b804-77c366188301",
                        "entry_id": "9733b3df-da4b-3793-bdcd-6a9f1e187a0b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "mężczyzna nie uznający norm moralnych"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c2354e05-4abd-34ed-bffc-3216e83a5c45",
                        "entry_id": "9733b3df-da4b-3793-bdcd-6a9f1e187a0b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "zwolennik immoralizmu"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6dcca84-6a9e-4e17-83df-09c27233ebe4",
                                "sense_id": "c2354e05-4abd-34ed-bffc-3216e83a5c45",
                                "text": "(…) Nietzsche pisze o filozofach, zwłaszcza niemieckich, iż „chcą także, swoim sposobem «poprawiać ludzkość» na własne podobieństwo (…) wierzą wszyscy jeszcze w «ideał»… Ja jestem pierwszym immoralistą”"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "373da2ae-ac0f-43f1-b784-68f19d9331ca",
                        "source_entry_id": "9733b3df-da4b-3793-bdcd-6a9f1e187a0b",
                        "source_sense_id": "664b7f94-03c9-3354-b804-77c366188301",
                        "target_lang_word": "immoralist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "immoralist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b82f6555-1da6-33c2-a0f9-858ce8c2763c",
                                        "entry_id": "5980d31f-680d-3902-936d-b48a9c0eafcb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An advocate of immorality"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "139bf19e-362b-458c-a885-d1ac8f4ae53d",
                                                "sense_id": "b82f6555-1da6-33c2-a0f9-858ce8c2763c",
                                                "text": "WHEN it comes to poking serious fun at High Society and making a quiet mockery of its hypocritical ways there’s still no one one^([sic]) to match the Victorian age’s master of homosexual immorality, Mr Oscar Wilde. […] Wilde, being a first-class subversive, implies that the Wicked Lady, an unshamed adventureress and serial lover, ought be admired for the courage of her convictions: by contrast he mocks the aristocrats as immoralists desperate to be caught in a good light."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66a102c2-57ba-392f-9ab6-2bea08d6edda",
                                        "entry_id": "5980d31f-680d-3902-936d-b48a9c0eafcb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An adherent or practitioner of immoralism"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b979550a-a7e3-4c53-8d6e-507594a00205",
                        "source_entry_id": "9733b3df-da4b-3793-bdcd-6a9f1e187a0b",
                        "source_sense_id": "664b7f94-03c9-3354-b804-77c366188301",
                        "target_lang_word": "immoraliste",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "immoraliste",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11d0f8de-65f9-329e-923a-901dd0f417fe",
                                        "entry_id": "91f6a0c2-240a-33dd-8c63-b0d8f12182ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qui relève de l’immoralisme, qui ne se fonde par sur la morale établie ou la morale chrétienne."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd3bc962-b086-453d-a88b-1fa00714bd37",
                                                "sense_id": "11d0f8de-65f9-329e-923a-901dd0f417fe",
                                                "text": "De tout temps, l'Eglise a voulu anéantir ses ennemis : nous, les immoralistes et les antéchrists, nous trouvons avantage à ce que l'Eglise existe..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "immoraliste",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34472839-8dd7-3f1a-8afc-646a9c80451f",
                                        "entry_id": "e9b03c94-21ed-353c-8eba-4452352fa399",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Adepte de l’immoralisme, personne qui ne se fonde pas sur la morale établie ou la morale chrétienne."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c6640b9-d4ac-4cb9-a71a-775470b307ab",
                                                "sense_id": "34472839-8dd7-3f1a-8afc-646a9c80451f",
                                                "text": "Il agit contre la morale traditionnelle et apparaît comme un immoraliste absolu, ou plutôt comme quelqu'un qui sait habilement se jouer des règles de la société bien-pensante."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
